      "seed": 1650338867,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 346553017,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1795149935429,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "id": "sum_takeaway_body",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1362,
      "y": 1329,
      "width": 626,
      "height": 94,
      "text": "1. HOST = 1 Linux machine. SESSION = 1 virtual device (N per Host).\n2. Inside 1 device, AOSP shares system_server across apps — but duplicates\n   the ENTIRE OS across parallel VMs.\n3. ACOS keeps apps + framework + ART real, replaces system_server with a\n   4.5 MiB Rust Session Controller, and hoists heavy pools/engines to Host ONCE.\n4. Result: 20 parallel Android sessions fit in <1 GiB RAM total.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. HOST = 1 Linux machine. SESSION = 1 virtual device (N per Host).\n2. Inside 1 device, AOSP shares system_server across apps — but duplicates\n   the ENTIRE OS across parallel VMs.\n3. ACOS keeps apps + framework + ART real, replaces system_server with a\n   4.5 MiB Rust Session Controller, and hoists heavy pools/engines to Host ONCE.\n4. Result: 20 parallel Android sessions fit in <1 GiB RAM total.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
